# suspend_gap_every_key: A blob setting every register, the root FIFO disabled, at binary version 237 (connection types are checked from 238, so key 21 = 2 passes): after rvg_device_did_resume the registers show what the blob restored and what it did not. The pending display and stamp interrupt bits (keys 9, 10) read back once (read-to-clear); the fault key 11 is ignored (0x102c 0); the EFI registers 0x1210-0x121c and 0x1228 read the blob's values though EFI stays off; the connection types are not restored. 0x1000 = 1 alone then creates the root FIFO from the blob's base, length and start, with fresh counts (not keys 6 and 7): a NOP at the ring's start runs.
